<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερηνορ-έων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>exceedingly manly</i>: but always used in bad sense
			(though <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνορέη</span> is 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρεία</span>
			, <i>manliness, courage), overbearing, overweening,</i> of
			the Trojans, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.176
			</span></i>; of Deïphobus (the Trojan), <i><span class="en">
				13.258
			</span></i>; of the Cyclopes, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.5
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> mostly of the suitors, <i><span class="en">
				17.482
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶς ὑπερηνορέοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.266
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.766
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Com.,
				<i>thinking oneself more than man,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				53
			</span></i>. (No Verb <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερηνορέω</span>
			occurs: cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερμενέων.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
